# Line endings.
#
# Every checkout of this repository is on Windows, so the working tree is CRLF while git
# keeps LF in the index - the normal arrangement, verified with `git ls-files --eol`.
# `text` with `eol=crlf` states both halves explicitly, so an editor or script that writes
# LF cannot leave the tree mixed and turn a one-line change into a whole-file diff.
#
# Text and binary are declared by extension instead of being inferred. An earlier attempt
# at normalising the tree leaned on git's `binary` attribute to decide per file and got
# its meaning backwards twice - `binary: unspecified` is the NORMAL state for text, and
# only `binary: set` marks a binary - which ran eight tracked PNGs through a line-ending
# rewrite and corrupted them on two separate runs, both restored from git. Listing the
# binary types removes the need to interpret that attribute at all.
* text eol=crlf

# Never line-ending convert these. The map images are licensed art and the exported PNGs
# are measurement evidence, so one altered byte matters more than a tidy diff.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.dll binary
*.pdb binary
*.ico binary
*.zip binary

# Patch and diff output stays exactly as produced.
*.patch -text
*.diff -text
